A workloop drain must not dereference the anonymous wlh sentinel, which killed trustd.

DISPATCH_INVOKE_WORKLOOP_DRAIN is supposed to imply that the draining thread adopted the workloop
as its wlh, so both sites below cast the wlh TSD straight to a dispatch_workloop_t and read
dwl_drained_qos out of it. This build sets DISPATCH_USE_KEVENT_WORKLOOP=0, nothing ever adopts a
wlh, and _dispatch_get_wlh therefore answers DISPATCH_WLH_ANON, which is (void *) ~0x3ul.

Measured: trustd is the only daemon on the roster that uses a dispatch workloop
(SecTrustServerGetWorkloop is its XPC target queue), and it took SIGSEGV on the load at
_dispatch_lane_serial_drain+499 after serving EVERY trust evaluation. RIP page offset 0x8f3 on
every crash, CR2 0x38, and RAX 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC, which is -4 plus the 0x3c field offset. Its
launchd LastExitStatus was 139.

_dispatch_wlh_to_workloop is libdispatch's own helper for exactly this and already answers NULL for
both NULL and the sentinel, so use it and skip the comparison when there is no workloop to compare
against. _dispatch_source_invoke already carried a hand rolled guard for the same sentinel, under
an ifdef DARLING that this build does not define.

After: five pokes, five replies, LastExitStatus 0 on all five, zero faults in ciderd.log, and ONE
trustd serving all five rather than five that each died.
--- a/src/queue.c
+++ b/src/queue.c
@@ -3678,8 +3678,13 @@
 			break;
 		}
 		if (likely(flags & DISPATCH_INVOKE_WORKLOOP_DRAIN)) {
-			dispatch_workloop_t dwl = (dispatch_workloop_t)_dispatch_get_wlh();
-			if (unlikely(_dispatch_queue_max_qos(dwl) > dwl->dwl_drained_qos)) {
+			// THE FLAG DOES NOT IMPLY A REAL WLH HERE. It is supposed to: only a thread that
+			// adopted the workloop sets WORKLOOP_DRAIN. With DISPATCH_USE_KEVENT_WORKLOOP=0
+			// nothing ever adopts one, so the plain cast dereferenced the DISPATCH_WLH_ANON
+			// sentinel (~0x3) and trustd died on this line after serving every trust evaluation.
+			// No workloop means no drained_qos to compare against, so keep draining.
+			dispatch_workloop_t dwl = _dispatch_wlh_to_workloop(_dispatch_get_wlh());
+			if (dwl && unlikely(_dispatch_queue_max_qos(dwl) > dwl->dwl_drained_qos)) {
 				break;
 			}
 		}
@@ -5365,9 +5370,10 @@
 	if (unlikely(_dispatch_needs_to_return_to_kernel())) {
 		_dispatch_return_to_kernel();
 	}
+	// Same missing wlh guard as the drain loop above, on the channel path.
 	if (likely(dcic->dcic_flags & DISPATCH_INVOKE_WORKLOOP_DRAIN)) {
-		dispatch_workloop_t dwl = (dispatch_workloop_t)_dispatch_get_wlh();
-		if (unlikely(_dispatch_queue_max_qos(dwl) > dwl->dwl_drained_qos)) {
+		dispatch_workloop_t dwl = _dispatch_wlh_to_workloop(_dispatch_get_wlh());
+		if (dwl && unlikely(_dispatch_queue_max_qos(dwl) > dwl->dwl_drained_qos)) {
 			dcic->dcic_tq = dch->do_targetq;
 			return false;
 		}
